From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: refresh config.sub before configure (macOS 15 / Darwin 24)

On macOS 15 the build triplet from `clang -dumpmachine` is
`arm64-apple-darwin24.6.0`. Many old autotools contrib packages (dvdcss,
dvdread, dvdnav, a52, dca, libmpeg2, lame, opus, ...) ship a config.sub that
predates Apple-Silicon `arm64` support, so configure aborts with
"config.sub arm64-apple-darwin24.6.0 failed". Only ~30 packages call
$(UPDATE_AUTOCONFIG); the rest rely on their bundled config.sub.

Make the shared MAKECONFIGURE macro refresh config.sub/config.guess from the
host automake first, so every autotools package gets an arm64-aware config.sub.
This is a no-op where a fresh config.sub is already present, and harmless on
non-Darwin toolchains.
---
--- a/contrib/src/main.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/main.mak
@@ -453,7 +453,7 @@
 MAKEBUILDDIR = mkdir -p $(BUILD_DIR) && rm -f $(BUILD_DIR)/config.status
 MAKEBUILD = $(MAKE) -C $(BUILD_DIR)
 MAKECONFDIR = cd $(BUILD_DIR) && $(HOSTVARS) $(BUILD_SRC)
-MAKECONFIGURE = $(MAKECONFDIR)/configure $(HOSTCONF)
+MAKECONFIGURE = $(UPDATE_AUTOCONFIG) && $(MAKECONFDIR)/configure $(HOSTCONF)
 
 # Work around for https://lists.nongnu.org/archive/html/bug-gnulib/2020-05/msg00237.html
 # When using a single command, make might take a shortcut and fork/exec
